window.products.push({"id":80045,"name":"WP660532 Coil Replacement For Whirlpool Stove Range 660532 6 Inch Surface Element AP6010189 FES310BL1 RF263LXTB3 RF365PXMQ0 RF261PXST0 RF261PXST1 WFC1","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":10.95,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71y-Ci-ggPS._AC_SL1500_.jpg","description":"💡 Whirlpool 660532 Surface Element - It's a high-quality exact equivalent for part numbers 14201046, 14210026, 1938218, 1938250, 1938252, 1938284, 1938305, 1938343, 1938355, 19950006, 309251, 3195919. WP660532 Coil Surface Element is compatible with Whirlpool, Admiral, Amana, Crosley, Estate, Hoover, Inglis, Jenn-Air, Kenmore, KitchenAid, Magic Chef, Maytag, Norge, Roper. Whirlpool Wp660532 Surface Element is made of high-quality materials, which ensures that it is durable and long-lasting. 🔧 DIY eTips Included - Not sure how to replace the part? Helpful information can be found on the page below. Scroll down to get more repair tips. Acquire valuable skills during the DIY repair project. 660532 Stove Top Coil Burner will help if your appliance element does not heat. Our, easy to install, \"plug-in\" part has four turns, which provides the best customer experience. Before the repair process be sure to unplug the stove from the electrical outlet. 💡 660532 6 Inch Surface Element is located on the top of the stove and is used to heat cookware placed on it. If your original coil has stopped working or is malfunctioning, this replacement coil can be used to restore your stove to its original working condition. The 660532 Surface Element fits hundred of models and can be easily installed. 1500W 4 Coil Electric Range Burner Element meets or exceeds all manufacturer specifications. We provide a lifetime warranty and guarantee 100% money back. 💡 Are stovetop elements universal? Stovetop elements are not universal, as they come in a variety of shapes, sizes, and wattages, and are designed to fit specific stovetop models. When purchasing a replacement stovetop element, it's important to ensure that it is the right size, shape, and wattage for your stovetop, otherwise it may not fit properly or heat up as intended. Additionally, different stovetop brands and models may require different types of stovetop elements. 💡 How long do burner elements last? The lifespan of burner elements can vary depending on several factors, including how often they are used, how well they are maintained, and the quality of the element itself. As a general rule of thumb, most burner elements will last anywhere from 5 to 15 years before needing to be replaced. Regular cleaning and maintenance of burner elements can help extend their lifespan by preventing buildup of food debris and other contaminants.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71y-Ci-ggPS._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"PartsBroz","source_asin":"B09RK8Q9LR","category_path":"Home & Appliances"},"sku":"BM-80045","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B09RK8Q9LR","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Appliances.jsonl","source_asin":"B09RK8Q9LR","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
